Alkali and alkaline earth metals react with water to produce hydrogen gas and metal hydroxide. This is due to their high electropositive character.

\begin{aligned}
& 2 $\mathrm{Na}+$2 $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$ \rightarrow 2 $\mathrm{NaOH}+\mathrm{H}_2$ \\
& $\mathrm{Mg}+$2 $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$ \rightarrow $\mathrm{Mg}$($\mathrm{OH}$)_2+$\mathrm{H}_2$
\end{aligned}
